# Probe payload blobs. The observation JSONL and run manifest are committed --
# they carry hashes and sizes, not feed content -- but raw payloads are repo
# bloat with no evidential value beyond their hash.
scripts/probe/runs/*/blobs/
runs/*/blobs/

# Kill switch sentinel
STOP

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local Claude Code session settings. Holds machine-absolute interpreter paths
# and session-scoped scratchpad paths, so it is local state, not project
# configuration. Ignored rather than left untracked: a repo that claims to
# rebuild from git gets one accidental `git add -A` away from committing a path
# that only exists on one machine. Anything here that should be shared gets
# split into a tracked file deliberately.
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# Credential-shaped paths that turn up in a project directory by accident.
#
# The backstop, not the control. Secrets are SOPS + age; nothing here should
# ever exist in the working tree in the first place. This section is for the
# mistake that has already happened once: on 2026-08-29 an AWS `credentials`
# file was created at `.aws/credentials` inside this repo rather than in
# `~/.aws`. It was caught by inspection before any commit -- not by a gate.
#
# Read `docs/limits.md` before trusting this. The structural check would not
# have stopped that commit, and one of the two reasons has since been fixed:
#
#   - STILL TRUE: it walks tracked files, so an untracked credential in the
#     working tree is invisible to it. That is the half that is still open.
#   - NO LONGER TRUE, closed in df63680: the key=value rule was gated on file
#     suffix, so an extensionless `credentials` file was scanned and then
#     exempted from the one rule that would have fired. It now runs on every
#     scannable file. This comment asserted the old behaviour for three commits
#     after it stopped being true -- corrected 2026-08-29 after review 6's O1.
#
# An ignore rule is still what stands between `git add -A` and a pushed key,
# because the tracked-file scan cannot see the file until the commit that adds
# it. `git add -f` overrides an ignore rule; this is a backstop, not a gate.
.aws/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.ppk
id_rsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*credentials*.csv

# Terraform.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the provider pin --
# exact versions plus hashes -- and CLAUDE.md requires every version pinned, so
# it is committed and reviewed like any other lock file.
#
# Bootstrap state is local by construction (ADR 0007) and must never be
# committed: it is the one state file with nowhere else to live, and a tracked
# .tfstate would also fail the credential gate's coverage test, since .tfstate
# is not a scannable suffix. That failure is correct -- it forces the decision
# rather than letting state drift into git.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
crash.log
crash.*.log
